  <steps>
    <step>Create invoiceService.createInvoice mirroring workAssignmentService: discover sprk_invoice nav-props, build payload from the manifest (sprk_invoicedate default today), BU defaults, applyResolverFields (Matter/Project), createRecord('sprk_invoice'), file pipeline with dual-bind (Invoice + host via createDocumentRecords additionalBinds), warnings.</step>
    <step>Create CreateInvoiceWizard wrapping CreateRecordWizard: associateToStep config, CreateInvoiceStep (Enter Info with useAiPrefill wired but prefillEnabled=false), Next Steps cards (Send Email/Add To Do/Assign Work) via WizardFollowOns.</step>
    <step>Wire wizardRegistry 'invoice' → CreateInvoiceWizard (replace placeholder from task 011).</step>
    <step>Unit tests per ADR-038.</step>
  </steps>

  <tools>Read, Grep, Edit, Write, Skill(adr-check), Skill(code-review)</tools>
  <outputs>components/CreateInvoiceWizard/ + registry entry + tests.</outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion>Submitting creates a valid sprk_invoice regarding the host with all resolver fields.</criterion>
    <criterion>Enter Info collects exactly the manifest fields; invoicedate defaults to today.</criterion>
    <criterion>Uploaded file dual-binds (host + Invoice subgrids).</criterion>
    <criterion>Prefill seam present but inert; adr-check clean.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Invoice create from host visual">
      <steps><step>Open an Invoice-bound visual on a Matter</step><step>Click "+"; complete wizard; submit</step><step>Inspect the Invoice regarding + resolver fields</step></steps>
      <expected>Valid sprk_invoice regarding the host; no console errors</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <notes>
    <completion-summary>
      Completed 2026-07-08. Built CreateInvoiceWizard end-to-end under
      src/client/shared/Spaarke.UI.Components/src/components/CreateInvoiceWizard/:
      formTypes.ts, invoiceService.ts, CreateInvoiceStep.tsx, CreateInvoiceWizard.tsx,
      index.ts, plus 3 test files under __tests__/ (23 tests, all passing).

      invoiceService.createInvoice mirrors workAssignmentService.createWorkAssignment
      exactly: nav-prop discovery (sprk_invoice + sprk_document) -> manifest payload
      (sprk_invoicenumber/sprk_name/sprk_description/sprk_vendororg bind/sprk_invoicedate
      defaulting to today) -> BU cascade (applyUserBuDefaults) -> applyResolverFields
      (Matter/Project host regarding, ADR-024 5-field write) -> createRecord('sprk_invoice')
      -> file pipeline with dual-bind (Invoice primary + host additionalBinds via
      createDocumentRecords) -> warnings array, never throws.

      CreateInvoiceWizard.tsx wraps CreateRecordWizard: associateToStep uses new
      INVOICE_REGARDING_TARGETS (Matter+Project only, added to AssociateToStep/types.ts
      per the Phase-0 manifest — narrower than Event's 9-entity list), CreateInvoiceStep
      for Enter Info (useAiPrefill wired via PREFILL_ENABLED=false inert seam — verified
      by test: no spinner, no network call), and a CUSTOM Next Steps card set
      (Send Email / Add To Do / Assign Work) via a new opt-in `followOnCards?:
      FollowOnCardConfig[]` override added to ICreateRecordWizardConfig
      (CreateRecordWizard/types.ts + one-line consumption change in
      CreateRecordWizard.tsx: `cards={config.followOnCards ?? followOnCards}`).
      This was necessary because CreateRecordWizard's built-in default card set
      (Assign Work/Create Event/Send Email) doesn't include Add To Do — required by
      this task's spec — and forking CreateRecordWizard or hand-rolling a 5th wizard
      directly on WizardShell would have duplicated more scaffolding than the override.
      Fully backward compatible: existing consumers (CreateEventWizard, CreateMatterWizard,
      CreateProjectWizard) don't pass followOnCards and are unaffected (regression-tested).
      CreateInvoiceWizard owns all 3 follow-on cards' state locally via refs (mirroring
      WorkAssignmentWizardDialog.tsx/SummarizeFilesDialog.tsx's established pattern) and
      reads it directly in onFinish rather than via IFinishContext.followOn (documented
      explicitly in the followOnCards JSDoc as a footgun for future maintainers).
      Also widened FollowOnActionId to `... | (string & {})` for backward-compatible
      typing of non-default card ids.

      Wired wizardRegistry.ts: `invoice` key now imports CreateInvoiceWizard (was
      PlaceholderWizard). Added CreateInvoiceWizard barrel export to components/index.ts.

      Quality gates: code-review (clean — 0 Critical, 1 Warning re: file-size/footgun
      both assessed as acceptable-by-design, 1 informational note re: pre-existing
      unrelated wizardRegistry.test.ts failure caused by a concurrent task's rename)
      and adr-check (clean — ADR-024/012/021/038 all compliant) both passed unconditionally
      per FULL rigor. `tsc --noEmit` clean; full regression suite for all touched shared
      consumers passes.

      Note: this task ran concurrently with task 040 (CreateReportCardWizard, formerly
      "kpi-assessment") editing the same shared files (wizardRegistry.ts,
      CreateRecordWizard.tsx/types.ts, components/index.ts). Both tasks' additive
      changes coexist cleanly (verified via re-run of typecheck + tests after each
      concurrent edit landed) — no conflicts.
    </completion-summary>
  </notes>
</task>
